 "transcript": [
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Well, and I suppose they will eat my flesh and drink my blood one day if they are not content with the flesh and blood of the two young slaves of mine.\"",
  "[says] (to Wang Lung) The eldest son says they are not so greedy.",
  "the eldest son (to Wang Lung): \"Well, and it is not so with our sons. It is with me and with my wife and with our slaves and with the children of our servants and with our servants and our slaves that we live, and it is not the sons of ours who live in the great house and who live on rice and meat and on the best of everything and who live in luxury and with a hundred slaves and with a thousand servants.\"",
  "[action] The sons argue over their father's land and money.",
  "the eldest son: \"Well, and we are not so greedy, and we are content with our lot. Our elder son is content with his wife and he is content with the land we have, and we are not greedy, and we are content with our lot.\"",
  "[silence] the second son says nothing.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son, the second son): \"Well, and you are my sons and I will not have you fighting over my land. You are both to have it as I did, and neither of you will know that the other is there.\"",
  "[silence] the second son says nothing.",
  "[says] Wang Lung expresses his confusion and annoyance.",
  "[action] (to the second son) The eldest son and his brother argue over their father's land.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung stops them from fighting.",
